This paper investigates the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \Delta^2u-\beta\Delta u=\left(\frac{1}{|x|^\alpha}*F(u)\right)f(u),\quad\mbox{in}\ \ \mathbb{R}^4,
  \end{array}
  \right.
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} under specific conditions and when the nonlinearity exhibits exponential growth. Using a combination of the mountain pass theorem and a uniformity lemma, we demonstrate the existence of a normalized ground state solution for this equation.

